 "_description": "Manifest.chunk_count records the PRE-dedup chunk count captured at extraction time; chunks.json reflects the POST-dedup (cross-file, content-hash) final count. build_index() never writes back the post-dedup count to manifest.json, so any file that contributed a cross-file duplicate desyncs permanently. This is a known, accepted debt (not yet fixed) -- aria_rag.check treats exactly these paths as pass, and fails on any NEW desync not in this list. Paths are relative to Settings.docs_dir (Ressources/), forward-slash, for portability. Regenerated after adding REG2A10_1DE2.pdf as validity=superseded (MS1 pair inventory follow-up): REG2A10_1DE2_MS1.pdf is no longer desynced (it now legitimately holds all 1636 chunks, its former competitor REG2A10_1DE2.pdf being excluded from indexing entirely), so its entry -- added during the Stage A ripple-effect fix -- is dropped. No new desync appeared this round. Regenerated again after the table-chunker fix (CH-06): REG2A1_MS1.pdf and both REG2A10_*.pdf's counts changed (fine-grained row/entry chunks instead of 1200-char windows -- see indexer.chunk_text_by_table) and now contribute a handful of cross-file content-hash duplicates each (e.g. short, identically-worded running-header-only fragments), same known shape as every other entry here. Regenerated again 2026-09-19 after the Docling section-aware batch ingestion of annexes/oap/rapport_presentation/padd (scratch/ingest_families_docling.py) -- 28 new entries, all the same shape (a handful of short cross-file duplicate chunks, e.g. running headers/legends repeated verbatim across an atlas's plate files, deduped by content hash), same known/accepted debt.",
